{
  "info": {
    "name": "Enerza API",
    "description": "Load-shedding and power-outage management API (25 endpoints).\n\n**How to use**\n1. Set `baseUrl` (default `http://localhost:5000/api/v1`) and, if your seed used different ones, `adminEmail` / `adminPassword`.\n2. Run the three *Login as …* requests in **Auth**: they save `adminToken`, `technicianToken` and `customerToken`.\n3. Run the folders top to bottom. Requests save the ids later requests need (`feederId`, `scheduleId`, `outageId`, `billId`, `paymentId`).\n\nThe collection's pre-request script looks up the seeded grid ids (`zoneId`, `substationId`, `areaId`, …) from the public feeder list and sets `{{tomorrow}}` and `{{thisMonth}}` in Asia/Dhaka time.\n\nEach request's description states the expected status and the other outcomes it can return.\n\nFor the multipart requests, pick your own image file in the `profilePhoto` / `photo` field.\n\n**Response format**\n- success: `{ success: true, statusCode, message, data, meta? }`\n- error: `{ success: false, statusCode, message, errors: [{ path, message }] }`",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Auth",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Register a customer",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Rahim Uddin\",\n  \"email\": \"rahim@example.com\",\n  \"password\": \"Rahim@12345\",\n  \"contactNumber\": \"01712345678\",\n  \"areaId\": \"{{areaId}}\",\n  \"meterNumber\": \"MTR-200001\",\n  \"connectionType\": \"RESIDENTIAL\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/register",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "auth",
                "register"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Expected: **201**. Creates a customer account with its service connection (area + meter) and sends a welcome email. `areaId` is filled in by the collection's pre-request script (Pallabi).\n\nOther outcomes:\n- **409** Email already registered\n- **400** Validation failed"
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Login as admin",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (body.data && body.data.accessToken) {",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set(\"adminToken\", body.data.accessToken);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{adminEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{adminPassword}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/login",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "auth",
                "login"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Expected: **200**. Saves `adminToken`. The admin account is created by the seed from `ADMIN_EMAIL` / `ADMIN_PASSWORD`; set the collection variables `adminEmail` and `adminPassword` to match.\n\nOther outcomes:\n- **401** Wrong password"
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Login as technician",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (body.data && body.data.accessToken) {",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set(\"technicianToken\", body.data.accessToken);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"tech.south@enerza.com\",\n  \"password\": \"Enerza@12345\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/login",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "auth",
                "login"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Expected: **200**. Saves `technicianToken` (the Dhaka South technician)."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Login as customer",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (body.data && body.data.accessToken) {",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set(\"customerToken\", body.data.accessToken);",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set(\"refreshToken\", body.data.refreshToken);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"customer2@enerza.com\",\n  \"password\": \"Enerza@12345\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/login",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "auth",
                "login"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Expected: **200**. Saves `customerToken` and `refreshToken` (customer2, a commercial connection in Dhanmondi 27)."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Login with Google",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"idToken\": \"not-a-real-google-id-token\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/google",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "auth",
                "google"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Expected: **200** with a real Google ID token. Body: `{ idToken }`, the ID token the browser gets from Google Sign-In for this app's `GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID`. A valid token logs the customer in (creating the account on first use) and returns the same shape as the password login. A real token cannot be stored in a collection, so only the error cases are saved here.\n\nOther outcomes:\n- **401** Invalid Google token\n- **400** Missing token"
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Refresh token",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (body.data && body.data.accessToken) {",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set(\"customerToken\", body.data.accessToken);",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set(\"refreshToken\", body.data.refreshToken);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"refreshToken\": \"{{refreshToken}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh-token",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "auth",
                "refresh-token"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Expected: **200**. Takes the refresh token from the body or from the `refreshToken` cookie.\n\nOther outcomes:\n- **401** Invalid refresh token"
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ],
      "description": "Registration, login (password and Google) and token refresh under `/api/v1/auth`. The three *Login as …* requests save `adminToken`, `technicianToken` and `customerToken`."
    },
    {
      "name": "Users",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Get my profile",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (body.data && body.data.customer) {",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set(\"customerId\", body.data.customer.id);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{customerToken}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/users/me",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "users",
                "me"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Expected: **200**. Any logged-in user. Never returns the password.\n\nOther outcomes:\n- **401** No token"
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Update my profile",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
