    {
      "name": "Feeders",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Create a feeder (admin)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (body.data && body.data.id) {",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set(\"feederId\", body.data.id);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{adminToken}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Banani Road 11 Feeder\",\n  \"code\": \"FD-BAN-01\",\n  \"loadMW\": 6.5,\n  \"priority\": \"NORMAL\",\n  \"substationId\": \"{{substationId}}\",\n  \"areas\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Banani\",\n      \"code\": \"AR-BANANI\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Kakoli\",\n      \"code\": \"AR-KAKOLI\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/feeders",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "feeders"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Expected: **201**. Creates the feeder and its areas in one transaction. Saves `feederId`. Audited.\n\nOther outcomes:\n- **409** Code already in use\n- **403** Technician is not allowed\n- **400** Validation failed\n- **401** No token"
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "List feeders (public)",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/feeders?searchTerm=mirpur&isActive=true&page=1&limit=5&sortBy=loadMW&sortOrder=desc",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "feeders"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "searchTerm",
                  "value": "mirpur"
                },
                {
                  "key": "isActive",
                  "value": "true"
                },
                {
                  "key": "page",
                  "value": "1"
                },
                {
                  "key": "limit",
                  "value": "5"
                },
                {
                  "key": "sortBy",
                  "value": "loadMW"
                },
                {
                  "key": "sortOrder",
                  "value": "desc"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Expected: **200**. No login needed. Filters: `searchTerm` (feeder or area name / code), `zoneId`, `substationId`, `priority`, `isActive`. Cached in Redis for 2 minutes; the `X-Cache` response header says HIT or MISS.\n\nOther outcomes:\n- **400** Invalid query"
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Update a feeder (admin)",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{adminToken}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"loadMW\": 7.25,\n  \"priority\": \"HIGH\",\n  \"areas\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Banani DOHS\",\n      \"code\": \"AR-BANANI-DOHS\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/feeders/{{feederId}}",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "feeders",
                "{{feederId}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Expected: **200**. Any of `name`, `loadMW`, `priority`, `isActive`; `areas` adds new areas. Audited with before and after values.\n\nOther outcomes:\n- **404** Feeder not found\n- **400** Invalid id"
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Delete a feeder (admin)",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{adminToken}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "method": "DELETE",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/feeders/{{feederId}}",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "feeders",
                "{{feederId}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Expected: **200**. Soft delete (`isDeleted`), together with the feeder's areas. Refused while the feeder still has customers, upcoming schedules or an open outage.\n\nOther outcomes:\n- **409** Feeder is still in use\n- **404** Already deleted"
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ],
      "description": "The grid's core resource under `/api/v1/feeders`: full CRUD with nested areas. The list is public and cached."
    },
    {
      "name": "Schedules",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Create a schedule (admin)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "const data = body.data || {};",
                  "const first = (data.schedules || data)[0] || data;",
                  "if (first && first.id) {",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set(\"scheduleId\", first.id);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{adminToken}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"type\": \"MAINTENANCE\",\n  \"feederIds\": [\n    \"{{maintenanceFeederId}}\"\n  ],\n  \"startTime\": \"{{tomorrow}}T10:00\",\n  \"endTime\": \"{{tomorrow}}T13:00\",\n  \"reason\": \"Transformer oil replacement\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/schedules",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "schedules"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Expected: **201**. Manual `LOAD_SHEDDING` or `MAINTENANCE` window on one or more feeders. Times without an offset are Asia/Dhaka. The feeder rows are locked while conflicts are checked, so two overlapping requests cannot both succeed. `{{tomorrow}}` is set by the collection's pre-request script. Saves `scheduleId`.\n\nOther outcomes:\n- **409** Overlaps an existing schedule\n- **400** Validation failed"
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Generate load shedding (admin)",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{adminToken}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"zoneId\": \"{{zoneId}}\",\n  \"date\": \"{{tomorrow}}\",\n  \"startHour\": 18,\n  \"endHour\": 22,\n  \"slotMinutes\": 60,\n  \"deficitMW\": 12,\n  \"dryRun\": true\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/schedules/generate",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "schedules",
                "generate"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Expected: **200**. Plans a fair rotation for a zone or a substation: CRITICAL feeders are never shed, LOW goes before NORMAL before HIGH, and within a priority the feeder shed least in the last 7 days goes first. No feeder is cut in two slots in a row or for more than 4 hours a day. `dryRun: true` (the default) only returns the plan; `false` saves it as DRAFT schedules.\n\nOther outcomes:\n- **400** Validation failed"
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "List schedules",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{adminToken}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/schedules?status=DRAFT&from={{tomorrow}}&page=1&limit=3&sortBy=startTime&sortOrder=asc",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "schedules"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "status",
                  "value": "DRAFT"
                },
                {
                  "key": "from",
                  "value": "{{tomorrow}}"
                },
                {
                  "key": "page",
                  "value": "1"
                },
                {
                  "key": "limit",
                  "value": "3"
                },
                {
                  "key": "sortBy",
                  "value": "startTime"
                },
                {
                  "key": "sortOrder",
                  "value": "asc"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Expected: **200**. Admin: every schedule, filtered by `type`, `status`, `phase` (UPCOMING / ONGOING / COMPLETED), `feederId`, `zoneId`, `from`, `to`. Customer: the published upcoming and ongoing schedules of their own feeder. `phase` is computed from the clock on every read.\n\nOther outcomes:\n- **403** Technician is not allowed"
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Publish or cancel a schedule (admin)",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{adminToken}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"status\": \"PUBLISHED\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/schedules/{{scheduleId}}/status",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "schedules",
                "{{scheduleId}}",
                "status"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Expected: **200**. `PUBLISHED` (from DRAFT) or `CANCELLED` (with an optional `reason`). Publishing emails a notice to the customers on that feeder. Audited.\n\nOther outcomes:\n- **409** Already cancelled\n- **404** Schedule not found"
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ],
      "description": "Load-shedding and maintenance schedules under `/api/v1/schedules`: manual creation, the fair generator, role-aware listing and publish / cancel."
    },
    {
      "name": "Outages",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Report or create an outage",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (body.data && body.data.outage) {",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set(\"outageId\", body.data.outage.id);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{customerToken}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"description\": \"No power in Dhanmondi 27 since 7 pm, the whole street is dark\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/outages",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "outages"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Expected: **201**. Customer: `{ description }`; the feeder comes from their area. `data.outcome` is one of `NEW_OUTAGE_CREATED`, `LINKED_TO_EXISTING_OUTAGE` or `EXPLAINED_BY_SCHEDULE`. Admin: `{ description, feederId }` logs an incident directly. The feeder row is locked, so a feeder never has two open outages. Saves `outageId`.\n\nA customer can attach a photo of the fault by sending `multipart/form-data`: `description` as a text field and the image in `photo` (JPEG, PNG or WebP, up to 5 MB). It is stored on Cloudinary and returned as `report.photoUrl`.\n\nOther outcomes:\n- **409** Customer already has an open report\n- **400** Validation failed"
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Change outage status",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{adminToken}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"status\": \"ASSIGNED\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/outages/{{outageId}}/status",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "outages",
                "{{outageId}}",
                "status"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Expected: **200**. The state machine: REPORTED → ASSIGNED → IN_PROGRESS → RESOLVED, with CANCELLED from REPORTED or ASSIGNED and reassignment from ASSIGNED or IN_PROGRESS. Admin: `ASSIGNED` (optional `technicianId`; without it the least-loaded available technician in the zone is picked) and `CANCELLED` (`note` required). Assigned technician: `IN_PROGRESS` and `RESOLVED` (`note` required). Every move writes a timeline row and an audit row. When an outage is resolved, the customers who reported it are emailed.\n\nOther outcomes:\n- **403** Technician cannot assign\n- **400** Transition not allowed\n- **404** Outage not found"
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "List outages",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{adminToken}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/outages?status=ASSIGNED&zoneId={{zoneId}}&page=1&limit=5&sortBy=priority&sortOrder=desc",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "outages"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "status",
                  "value": "ASSIGNED"
                },
                {
                  "key": "zoneId",
                  "value": "{{zoneId}}"
                },
                {
                  "key": "page",
                  "value": "1"
                },
                {
                  "key": "limit",
                  "value": "5"
                },
                {
                  "key": "sortBy",
                  "value": "priority"
                },
                {
                  "key": "sortOrder",
                  "value": "desc"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Expected: **200**. Admin: all outages. Technician: the ones assigned to them. Customer: the ones they reported, with their own report. Filters: `status`, `priority`, `feederId`, `zoneId`, `from`, `to`. Each outage includes its timeline.\n\nOther outcomes:\n- **401** No token"
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ],
      "description": "Outage reports and incidents under `/api/v1/outages`: intake with dedupe, the status state machine with technician assignment, and role-aware listing."
